---
import ServiceSection from "../components/ServiceSection.astro";
import Endpoint from "../components/Endpoint.astro";
import RustSchema from "../components/RustSchema.astro";
---

<ServiceSection id="service-toon">
  <Fragment slot="title"><code>Toon</code> — identity and bootstrap</Fragment>
<p>Toon endpoints provide the account's playable identities and global SC2
    bootstrap configuration.</p>
    <p class="endpoint-index">
      <a href="#toon-list">Toon/0 ToonList</a><a href="#toon-create">Toon/1–4 creation</a>
      <a href="#toon-select">Toon/5 ToonSelect</a><a href="#toon-selected">Toon/6 ToonSelected</a>
      <a href="#toon-created">Toon/7 and Toon/8 creation result</a><a href="#toon-welcome">Toon/10 Welcome</a>
      <a href="#toon-billing">Toon/13 BillingUpdate</a><a href="#toon-initial-complete">Toon/14 InitialNotifiesComplete</a>
      <a href="#toon-cais-time">Toon/23 CaisTimeUpdate</a>
    </p>

    <Endpoint id="toon-list" direction="server → client" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Toon/0</code> Toon::ToonList</Fragment>
      <p>Lists up to fifty toon display records owned by the authenticated account.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct ToonList {
    displays: Vec<ToonDisplay>, // count: 6 wire bits, 0..=50
}

struct ToonDisplay {
    name: String, // byte count: 7 bits, stored as len - 2; 2..=100 bytes
    last_online: i32,
    _reserved: Reserved<3>,
    flags: u32,
    profile: RecordAddress,
    realm: u32,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="toon-create" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Toon/1–4</code> toon creation exchange</Fragment>
      <p>The creation exchange begins with an empty Init request and empty Setup
      response. Final submits the desired display name. Cancel abandons the setup
      with an empty name.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server, Toon/1
struct ToonCreateInit;

// server → client, Toon/2
struct ToonCreateSetup;

// client → server, Toon/3
struct ToonCreateFinal {
    data: ToonCreationData,
}

struct ToonCreationData {
    display_name: String,
}

// client → server, Toon/4
struct ToonCreateCancel;`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="toon-select" direction="client → server" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="live verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Toon/5</code> Toon::ToonSelect</Fragment>
      <p>Selects one display returned by Toon/0 before channel discovery and join.
      A successful selection is followed by Toon/6.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct ToonSelect {
    toon_name: String,          // byte count: 7 bits, stored as len - 2
    generated_check: Bits<10>, // rolling check seeded with 2
    realm: u32,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">Reflection lists name then realm and omits the
      generated rolling check between them.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="toon-created" direction="server → client" phase="protected" structure="verified generated order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Toon/7</code> ToonCreated and <code>Toon/8</code> Failure</Fragment>
      <p>A successful creation returns the selected name, realm, and profile record
      address. Failure returns a catalog-backed error code.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct ToonCreated {
    toon_name: String,
    realm: u32,
    record_address: RecordAddress,
}

struct ToonCreationFailure {
    error: u16,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="toon-selected" direction="server → client" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="live verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Toon/6</code> Toon::ToonSelected</Fragment>
      <p>Confirms the active SC2 identity and returns its stable handle and profile
      address.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct ToonSelected {
    record_address: RecordAddress,
    toon_handle: ToonHandle,
    realm: u32,
    last_logon: i32,
    toon_name: String, // byte count: 7 bits, stored as len - 2
}

struct RecordAddress {
    label: u32,
    id: u64,
}

struct ToonHandle {
    program: FourCC,
    region: u8,
    realm: u32,
    id: u64,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="toon-billing" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Toon/13</code> Toon::BillingUpdateNotify</Fragment>
      <p>Reports game-account billing state. Captures show the official client
      emitting this route and the server-side type table also maps it inbound.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct BillingUpdateNotify {
    info: BillingInfo,
}

struct BillingInfo {
    units_remaining: Option<u32>,
    subscription_expires: Option<i32>,
    flags: u32,
    box_level: u8,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The generated <code>BillingInfo</code> order is
      <code>flags</code>, 19 filler bits, <code>subscription_expires</code>, 28
      filler bits, <code>units_remaining</code>, then <code>box_level</code>.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="toon-welcome" direction="server → client" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Toon/10</code> Toon::Welcome</Fragment>
      <p>Supplies global client configuration. Its generated layout reorders
      reflected members and consumes filler runs.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct Welcome {
    depot_region: FourCC,
    achievement_handles: Vec<AchievementHandle>, // count: 0..=15
    is_playing_from_igr: bool,
    default_portrait: u32,
    _reserved_0: Reserved<31>,
    max_game_server_connect_timeout_ms: u32,
    program_name: Vec<u8>,                         // 0..=32 bytes
    program_flags: Bits<128>,
    realm_map_list: Vec<RealmMap>,                 // count: 0..=4
    unlockables_files: Vec<UnlockableDefinition>, // count: 0..=128
    _reserved_1: Reserved<3>,
    max_map_favorites: u16,
    intermediate_name_restriction: String,         // 0..=1024 bytes
    final_name_restriction: String,                // 0..=1024 bytes
    current_time: i32,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="toon-initial-complete" direction="server → client" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="empty payload" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Toon/14</code> Toon::InitialNotifiesComplete</Fragment>
      <p>Marks completion of the initial Toon notification set.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct InitialNotifiesComplete; // zero payload bits`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="toon-cais-time" direction="client → server" phase="protected" structure="candidate reflected order" status="capture decoded, layout unverified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Toon/23</code> Toon::CaisTimeUpdate</Fragment>
      <p>Reports rested and played counters.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct CaisTimeUpdate {
    rested: u32,
    played: u32,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">Reflection order fits the current capture. This
      marked type currently has one source of evidence. Inspection output must
      continue to label it as a candidate layout pending independent verification.</p>
    </Endpoint>
</ServiceSection>
